    "pr_title": "Implement TCP keepalive support from RFC 1122",
    "pr_body": " Fixes zephyrproject-rtos#34044\r\n Signed-off-by:  Horse Ma <mawei@coltsmart.com>",
    "pr_comments": [
        "@maweicoltsmart Although the review process is intended to aid developers, I can imagine you are overwhelmed by the amount of review comments. \r\n\r\nSome tips you can used to check by yourself:\r\n\r\nRun the most prominent tests for TCP:\r\n./scripts/twister -T tests/net/socket/tcp -p qemu_x86\r\n./scripts/twister -T tests/net/tcp -p qemu_x86\r\n\r\nCheck your head commit before pushing against a lot of style rules\r\n./scripts/checkpatch.pl -g HEAD\r\n\r\nI hope this helps you with this and hopefully many more PRs",
        "This pull request has been marked as stale because it has been open (more than) 60 days with no activity. Remove the stale label or add a comment saying that you would like to have the label removed otherwise this pull request will automatically be closed in 14 days. Note, that you can always re-open a closed pull request at any time."
