    "issue_context": {
        "number": 34044,
        "title": "TCP connection does not support keepalive function",
        "body": "The keepalive function in tcp is very important. When will Zephyr OS support this function?",
        "comments": [
            "If the lwip protocol stack is transplanted, the network function of zephyr os will be more powerful.",
            "Indeed, the keepalive messages are currently not there. I cannot really say when they would be implemented. If you want that feature urgently, one option is to send a PR that fixes the issue. As always patches are welcome.\r\n",
            "> If the lwip protocol stack is transplanted, the network function of zephyr os will be more powerful.\r\n\r\nMay I ask why is that more powerful?",
            "For anyone that finds the above fork to implement TCP keepalive on their own -- there is a bug related to disconnects when using keepalive.  The tcp_conn_unref function is missing the lines to optionally cancel the keepalive_timer delayed task as part of its cleanup actions.  Since the memory is zeroed out afterwards, the reference is lost which can then result in \"jump to 0\" exceptions and hard faults on a disconnect.\r\n\r\nTake lines from here:\r\nhttps://github.com/maweicoltsmart/zephyr/commit/f1c5493faf26b809e4ed258cdae3dfd82bc314c3#diff-9ac8d59b0b68aecce1e4b98cae67d25e5f56a2a53c14316d30850f68f4e6a2f7R551-R553\r\n\r\nThen add those lines to here:\r\nhttps://github.com/maweicoltsmart/zephyr/commit/f1c5493faf26b809e4ed258cdae3dfd82bc314c3#diff-9ac8d59b0b68aecce1e4b98cae67d25e5f56a2a53c14316d30850f68f4e6a2f7R437",
            "I just wonder why #46716 was abandoned as it was quite near for merging. It is rather pointless to have keepalive support patches out-of-tree. @RBartonMesh would you be able to re-submit the patches with the fixes?\r\n",
            "ping @RBartonMesh / @maweicoltsmart if possible, please review / try #66316 "
        ]
    },
