            "review_comments": [
                "Do we really need all those `k_work_cancel_delayable(&conn->keepalive_timer);` sprinkled here and there across the code? I think it blurs the whole image. My understanding is, that once started, the keep-alive timer should be stopped only in 2 cases:\r\n* the keep-alive got disabled by the user on a socket (so inside `set_tcp_keep_alive()`)\r\n* or when the connection is being released (inside `tcp_conn_unref()`).\r\n",
                "Yes, this code is redundant and may cause keepalive to fail, I'll correct it right away."
